If you don't find anything soon I can start a dig in my CD collection.
What exactly do you need to know?

> 2.  What is the correct incantation to the boot rom to cause it to enter a 
> halt to
>      prom state >>> at boot?

something like >>> SET AUTO_ACTION HALT

> 6.  The CDROM is set to ID=4.  I would like to move it to ID=6, and add in a 
> few
>      more drive caddies.  Are there any gotchas in the hardware or NetBSD that
>      I need to be aware of to move it to ID=6?

Most, if not all, DEC CDROM drives for the Alpha series have the requirement
to be 512bytes/sector by default. But apart from that you can set the ID
to what you desire. I have my Alpha's CDs set to 6 as well. 

Just type BOOT DKA600 instead (assuming you see it as DKA400 now) to boot
from CD.

