An old DEC SWXCR.  Wonderful!
It's really a Mylex controller, as obvious by the probe message.  Nice
but a bit old, it'll give you 10-15 Mbyte/s throughput depending on
config.

NBs:
  * It can't address beyond ca 8Gbytes on disks that are larger than that.
  * RAID sets can't have more than 8 disks (but you can have several sets)
  * Volumes can't be made larger than about 32Gbytes (but you can make
    several from a set)

> Unfortunably all disks have been pulled out, so the mlx0 config is not in
>sync
> with the hardware. From what I can see from a show dev, it was configured
> with 6 disks:
>...

