On Thu, Jan 23, 2003 at 02:39:03PM +0100, sferriol wrote:

> >What version? 1.6? Or a -current snapshoot?
> 1.6
OK. You need to compile a TCWSCONS kernel to use local rasterconsole
and X11. 

> how can i know which graphic card i have on my dec???
It is written on the back of the card. Somthing like "PMAGB-BA"
Some DEC3k models have graphics build in, this is allways PMAGB-B / sfb.

> is there a command which display these informations??
Type at the SRM prompt:
show config
("sh conf" works also.)
You should post the output of this command and  / or /var/run/dmesg.boot 
to the list, if you have questions about speciffic devices.

> >>- ethernet
> >Build in ethernet works, the TC ethernet card works only in -current.
> same question, how can i know the type of my ethernet card??
There is only one TC ethernet card: PMAD-A :-)
Maybe you have some other card like FDDI or ATM that loks like 
Ethernet at the first glance. 

> when i installed the 1.6, there were no netbsd docs which specified the 
> console serial config.
> -> 9600 8N1 i suppose
9600 8n1 is a de facto standard. I have seen a lot of Unix machines and
console was every time 9600 BAUD, mostly 8n1, sometimes 7e1. Maybe 
only some real old machines like PDP-11 or PDP-8 use different settings. 
(Although my PDP-11/73 uses 9600 8n1 too. But this machine is quite young 
with its 15 years.) 
-- 



